"""If languages of two friends are same; what will happen to the program in problem 
6?"""

#Ans: If the languages of two friends are the same, the program will not be able to differentiate between the two friends based on their language preference. This can lead to confusion and incorrect results when trying to access or manipulate the data associated with each friend. It is important to ensure that each friend has a unique identifier (such as a unique name or ID) to avoid such issues in the program.